    "native_visual_review_evidence": "KM871 original scan and preview review\n\nAll15 native blocks,27 input terminals,8 external input labels,3 latch output references and all fields/pins/wedges read from native crops. Printed BB grid2A retained at physical normal2B position; root independently confirms this readable source contradiction and card0494A1. Other card/socket portions corroborated by A1, with no wiring inference. Normal bank calibration uses native left borders3967,4805,5622,6458,7292 at same top-row, consistent23-column pitch; apparent fourth-bank shift was an input-label/border misreading, no shift exists or applied.\n\nThree paired AND/OR inhibit latches traced separately. BB two output pins are separate nets. CB.B07 joins rail109 feeding DB.D10/B12, DF.B03 and DK.D04. CLOCKP0 rail114 feeds DF.B05 and DK.B09 through native diamond row40; it crosses feedback rail113 without joining. Each FB/FF/FK complement output uses a separate top feedback loop to DC.D09/DG.B09/DL.D09. OR outputs join their corresponding inverter input at native diamond161 then turn down to external references. Unlabeled AND output connectors and OR top connector retained; lower L latch markers are standalone printed glyphs at c138, with continuous wire after them into unlabeled physical input at c142. Calibrated native L glyph center6298 against normal OR border6452 and unit/grid first-character center6480 at c143: five native character pitches from L to first interior glyph, confirming c138 rather than c141. Native numeric control prefixes4D06/4B07/4B05 retained separately from wedges.\n\nNative sign spacing is literal: -GT and +RESTART/+CLOCK have no post-sign blank; + WRD labels do. Output names have -INHBT immediately after polarity. Title/date/log/part/revisions inspected independently:02-26-71,LOG983,FRAME02,MACH.7201-02,2586355,SDD BLK FL; EC05-01-70 713674 /10-19-70 714945 /02-01-71 714952. Printed page identity KM871 appears in header and vertical footer. User-approved P.N. label and right machine/part blank preserved.\n\nFull regenerated JuliaMono preview compared to native overview and native gate/pin/crossing crops. All source diamonds visible, no invented bend diamonds or joined crossings. Geometry/input-owner/allowed-character checks pass. No unreadable print remains.\n"
